txt\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1470\\\">-coordinate</span></div><span class=\\\"txt\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1472\\\">&nbsp;to the&nbsp;</span><div class=\\\"bundle\\\" style=\\\"display: inline-block; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\\\"><div class=\\\"expression variable\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1473\\\" style=\\\"position: relative; text-align: center; font-style: italic; display: inline-block;\\\"><span class=\\\"txt\\\">x</span></div><span class=\\\"txt\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1474\\\">-coordinate</span></div><span class=\\\"txt\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1476\\\">&nbsp;is&nbsp;</span><div class=\\\"bundle\\\" style=\\\"display: inline-block; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\\\"><div class=\\\"expression vFrac extraPadding\\\" data-testid=\\\"QMVerticalFraction\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1477\\\" style=\\\"position: relative; text-align: center; font-size: 14px; padding-left: 1px; padding-right: 0px; vertical-align: middle; display: inline-block;\\\"><div class=\\\"numerator\\\" role=\\\"group\\\" aria-label=\\\"3\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1464\\\"><span class=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\" data-testid=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\"><span class=\\\"expression number\\\" style=\\\"position: relative;\\\">3</span></span></div><div class=\\\"fracLine\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"divided by\\\" aria-roledescription=\\\"operator\\\" style=\\\"background-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); height: 1px; min-width: 10px;\\\"></div><div class=\\\"denominator\\\" role=\\\"group\\\" aria-label=\\\"2\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1465\\\"><span class=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\" data-testid=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\"><span class=\\\"expression number\\\" style=\\\"position: relative;\\\">2</span></span></div></div><span class=\\\"txt\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1478\\\">.</span></div></li></ul></div></div></div><p class=\\\"MsoListParagraph\\\" style=\\\"margin-top:13.7pt;margin-right:229.0pt;\\nmargin-bottom:0in;margin-left:23.95pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:105%;\\nmso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:23.85pt 23.95pt\\\"><span style=\\\"font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\\n11.0pt;line-height:105%;color:#363435;mso-font-width:115%\\\"></span></p><div class=\\\"secContentPiece\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1504\\\" style=\\\"margin-top: 16px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;IXL Verdana&quot;, Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\\\"><span class=\\\"txt\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1523\\\">So,</span><span class=\\\"txt\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1524\\\">&nbsp;the constant of proportionality is&nbsp;</span><div class=\\\"bundle\\\" style=\\\"display: inline-block; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\\\"><div class=\\\"expression vFrac extraPadding\\\" data-testid=\\\"QMVerticalFraction\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1525\\\" style=\\\"position: relative; text-align: center; font-size: 14px; padding-left: 1px; padding-right: 0px; vertical-align: middle; display: inline-block;\\\"><div class=\\\"numerator\\\" role=\\\"group\\\" aria-label=\\\"3\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1492\\\"><span class=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\" data-testid=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\"><span class=\\\"expression number\\\" style=\\\"position: relative;\\\">3</span></span></div><div class=\\\"fracLine\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"divided by\\\" aria-roledescription=\\\"operator\\\" style=\\\"background-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); height: 1px; min-width: 10px;\\\"></div><div class=\\\"denominator\\\" role=\\\"group\\\" aria-label=\\\"2\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1493\\\"><span class=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\" data-testid=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\"><span class=\\\"expression number\\\" style=\\\"position: relative;\\\">2</span></span></div></div><span class=\\\"txt\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1526\\\">.</span></div><span class=\\\"txt\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1528\\\">&nbsp;So, you can represent this relationship with the equation&nbsp;</span><div class=\\\"bundle\\\" style=\\\"display: inline-block; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\\\"><div class=\\\"expression typicalBinaryOperand\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1500\\\" style=\\\"position: relative; text-align: center; display: inline-block;\\\"><div class=\\\"expression variable\\\" style=\\\"position: relative; font-style: italic; display: inline-block;\\\"><span class=\\\"txt\\\">y</span></div></div><div class=\\\"expression binaryOperator equalsSymbolContainer\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"equals\\\" aria-roledescription=\\\"comparison symbol\\\" style=\\\"position: relative; text-align: center; margin-left: 6px; margin-right: 6px; display: inline-block;\\\"><span class=\\\"equalSymbol\\\">=</span></div></div><div class=\\\"bundle\\\" style=\\\"display: inline-block; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\\\"><div class=\\\"bundle\\\" data-last-child=\\\"true\\\" style=\\\"display: inline-block;\\\"><div class=\\\"expression typicalBinaryOperand\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1521\\\" style=\\\"position: relative; text-align: center; display: inline-block;\\\"><div class=\\\"expression contractedTimes\\\" style=\\\"position: relative; display: inline-block;\\\"><div class=\\\"expression vFrac\\\" data-testid=\\\"QMVerticalFraction\\\" style=\\\"position: relative; font-size: 14px; padding-left: 1px; padding-right: 1px; vertical-align: middle; display: inline-block;\\\"><div class=\\\"numerator\\\" role=\\\"group\\\" aria-label=\\\"3\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1517\\\"><span class=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\" data-testid=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\"><span class=\\\"expression number\\\" style=\\\"position: relative;\\\">3</span></span></div><div class=\\\"fracLine\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"divided by\\\" aria-roledescription=\\\"operator\\\" style=\\\"background-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); height: 1px; min-width: 10px;\\\"></div><div class=\\\"denominator\\\" role=\\\"group\\\" aria-label=\\\"2\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1518\\\"><span class=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\" data-testid=\\\"decimal-scalar\\\"><span class=\\\"expression number\\\" style=\\\"position: relative;\\\">2</span></span></div></div><div class=\\\"expression variable\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1534\\\" style=\\\"position: relative; font-style: italic; display: inline-block;\\\"><span class=\\\"txt\\\">x</span></div></div></div><span class=\\\"txt\\\" id=\\\"yui_3_18_1_1_1764216585602_1529\\\">.</span></div></div></div></span></div>\"}', '2025-11-27 01:33:00', '2025-11-27 03:24:40');
INSERT INTO `lesson_presentation_slides` (`id`, `lesson_presentation_id`, `section`, `slide_type`, `slide_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(10, 3, 'learn', 'text', '{\"text\": \"<b>Proportional Relationships – 10 Quick Multiple-Choice Questions</b>  \\n<br>Name: __________________________  \\n<br>\\n<br>Circle the correct answer.\\n<br>\\n<img src=\\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\" alt=\\\"\\\">1. Graph a&nbsp; – proportional?  \\n<br>   A) Yes   B) No  \\n<br>\\n2. Graph b&nbsp; – proportional?  \\n<br>   A) Yes   B) No  \\n<br>\\n<br>3. Taxi ride graph (problem 3) – proportional?  \\n<br>   A) Yes   B) No  \\n<br>\\n<br>4. Vacation driving graph (problem 4) – proportional?  \\n<br>   A) Yes   B) No  \\n<br>\\n<br>5. Point (1, 49) on vacation graph means:  \\n<br>   A) 1 mile in 49 hours  \\n<br>   B) 49 miles in 1 hour  \\n<br>   C) 49 miles in 49 hours  \\n<br>   D) 1 mile in 1 hour  \\n<br>\\n<br>6. Equation for vacation driving graph:  \\n<br>   A) y = 49x  B) y = x + 49  C) y = 49 – x  D) y = 49  \\n<br>\\n<br>7. Ice-skating tickets – constant of proportionality?  \\n<br>   A) $36  B) $18  C) $90  D) $162  \\n<br>\\n<br>8. Which store has the better DVD deal? (problem 6)  \\n<br>   A) Store A  B) Store B  C) Same price  \\n<br>\\n<br>9. Silver cost graph (problem 8) – proportional?  \\n<br>   A) Yes  B) No  \\n<br>\\n<br>10. Silver cost – price per pound?  \\n<br>    A) $17  B) $34  C) $68  D) $4  \\n<br>\\n<br><b>ANSWER KEY</b>  \\n<br>1. A 2. B 3. B 4. A 5. B 6. A 7. B 8. A 9. A 10. A\"}', '2025-11-27 03:24:41', '2025-11-27 03:24:41'),
(11, 3, 'learn', 'text', '{\"text\": \"<br>The graph below shows a proportional relationship between x and y.\\n<br>What is the constant of proportionality,&nbsp;<span class=\\\"katex\\\"><span class=\\\"katex-mathml\\\"><math xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\\\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\\\"true\\\" scriptlevel=\\\"0\\\"><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\\\"application/x-tex\\\">\\\\dfrac{y}{x}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\\\"katex-html\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><span class=\\\"base\\\"><span class=\\\"strut\\\" style=\\\"height:1.7936em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\\\"></span><span class=\\\"mord\\\"><span class=\\\"mopen nulldelimiter\\\"></span><span class=\\\"mfrac\\\"><span class=\\\"vlist-t vlist-t2\\\"><span class=\\\"vlist-r\\\"><span class=\\\"vlist\\\" style=\\\"height:1.1076em;\\\"><span style=\\\"top:-2.314em;\\\"><span class=\\\"pstrut\\\" style=\\\"height:3em;\\\"></span><span class=\\\"mord\\\"><span class=\\\"mord mathnormal\\\">x</span></span></span><span style=\\\"top:-3.23em;\\\"><span class=\\\"pstrut\\\" style=\\\"height:3em;\\\"></span><span class=\\\"frac-line\\\" style=\\\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\\\"></span></span><span style=\\\"top:-3.677em;\\\"><span class=\\\"pstrut\\\" style=\\\"height:3em;\\\"></span><span class=\\\"mord\\\"><span class=\\\"mord mathnormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-right:0.03588em;\\\">y</span></span></span></span><span class=\\\"vlist-s\\\">​ ?&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span class=\\\"vlist-r\\\"><span class=\\\"vlist\\\" style=\\\"height:0.686em;\\\"><br><img src=\\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" style=\\\"display: inline;\\\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>\"}', '2025-11-27 03:24:41', '2025-11-27 03:24:41'),
(12, 3, 'learn', 'text', '[]', '2025-11-27 03:24:42', '2025-11-27 03:24:42');
INSERT INTO `lesson_presentation_slides` (`id`, `lesson_presentation_id`, `section`, `slide_type`, `slide_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(13, 3, 'learn', 'text', '{\"text\": \"<h3><img src=\\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" style=\\\"color: rgb(55, 65, 81); font-size: 1rem;\\\"></h3>\\n<b>The graph shows the total cost for different weights of silver.</b>\\n<br><b>Fill in each blank. Use the graph to help you.\\n</b><br>1. When the weight is 0 pounds, the total cost is $______.  \\n<br>2. The graph passes through the point (______, ______). This is the origin.  \\n<br>3. The graph passes through the point (1, ______).  \\n<br>4. The constant of proportionality is ______ dollars per pound.  \\n<br>   (Hint: cost for 1 pound = ______ ÷ 1)  \\n<br>5. The point (2, 34) means 2 pounds cost $______.  \\n<br>   Price per pound = 34 ÷ ______ = $______.  \\n<br>6. The point (4, 68) means 4 pounds cost $______.  \\n<br>   Price per pound = 68 ÷ ______ = $______.  \\n<br>7. Because the graph is a _________________ that passes through _____________ and the ratio is always _________________,  \\n<br>   the relationship between weight and cost is __________________.  \\n<br>8. Write the equation that matches the graph (C = cost, w = weight in pounds):  \\n<br>   C = ______ × w  \\n<br>9. If someone buys 5 pounds of silver, the total cost will be $______.  \\n<br>   (Show work: ______ × 5 = ______)  \\n<br>10. If someone has $85, the maximum whole pounds of silver they can buy is ______ pounds.  \\n<br>    (Because ______ × ______ = 85)\\n<br>\\n<br><b>ANSWER KEY</b>  \\n<br><div><li>When the weight is 0 pounds, the total cost is $<strong>0</strong>.</li>\\n<li>The graph passes through the point (<strong>0</strong>, <strong>0</strong>). This is the origin.</li>\\n<li>The graph passes through the point (1, <strong>17</strong>).</li>\\n<li>The constant of proportionality is <strong>17</strong> dollars per pound.\\n(Hint: cost for 1 pound = <strong>17</strong> ÷ 1)</li>\\n<li>The point (2, 34) means 2 pounds cost $<strong>34</strong>.\\nPrice per pound = 34 ÷ <strong>2</strong> = $<strong>17</strong>.</li>\\n<li>The point (4, 68) means 4 pounds cost $<strong>68</strong>.\\nPrice per pound = 68 ÷ <strong>4</strong> = $<strong>17</strong>.</li>\\n<li>Because the graph is a <strong>straight line</strong> that passes through <strong>(0,0)</strong> and the ratio is always <strong>the same</strong>,\\nthe relationship between weight and cost is <strong>proportional</strong>.</li>\\n<li>Write the equation that matches the graph (C = cost, w = weight in pounds):\\nC = <strong>17</strong> × w</li>\\n<li>If someone buys 5 pounds of silver, the total cost will be $<strong>85</strong>.\\n(Show work: <strong>17</strong> × 5 = <strong>85</strong>)</li>\\n<li>If someone has $85, the maximum whole pounds of silver they can buy is <strong>5</strong> pounds.\\n(Because <strong>17</strong> × <strong>5</strong> = 85)</li></div>\"}', '2025-11-27 03:24:42', '2025-11-27 03:26:19'),
(14, 3, 'learn', 'text', '[]', '2025-11-27 03:24:42', '2025-11-27 03:24:42'),
(15, 3, 'learn', 'text', '{\"text\": \"<b>Proportional Relationships – 10 Quick Multiple-Choice Questions</b>  \\n<br>Name: __________________________  \\n<br>\\n<br>Circle the correct answer.\\n<br>\\n<img src=\\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\" alt=\\\"\\\">1. Graph a&nbsp; – proportional?  \\n<br>   A) Yes   B) No  \\n<br>\\n2. Graph b&nbsp; – proportional?  \\n<br>   A) Yes   B) No  \\n<br>\\n<br>3. Taxi ride graph (problem 3) – proportional?  \\n<br>   A) Yes   B) No  \\n<br>\\n<br>4. Vacation driving graph (problem 4) – proportional?  \\n<br>   A) Yes   B) No  \\n<br>\\n<br>5. Point (1, 49) on vacation graph means:  \\n<br>   A) 1 mile in 49 hours  \\n<br>   B) 49 miles in 1 hour  \\n<br>   C) 49 miles in 49 hours  \\n<br>   D) 1 mile in 1 hour  \\n<br>\\n<br>6. Equation for vacation driving graph:  \\n<br>   A) y = 49x  B) y = x + 49  C) y = 49 – x  D) y = 49  \\n<br>\\n<br>7. Ice-skating tickets – constant of proportionality?  \\n<br>   A) $36  B) $18  C) $90  D) $162  \\n<br>\\n<br>8. Which store has the better DVD deal? (problem 6)  \\n<br>   A) Store A  B) Store B  C) Same price  \\n<br>\\n<br>9. Silver cost graph (problem 8) – proportional?  \\n<br>   A) Yes  B) No  \\n<br>\\n<br>10. Silver cost – price per pound?  \\n<br>    A) $17  B) $34  C) $68  D) $4  \\n<br>\\n<br><b>ANSWER KEY</b>  \\n<br>1. A 2. B 3. B 4. A 5. B 6. A 7. B 8. A 9. A 10. A\"}', '2025-11-27 03:30:40', '2025-11-27 03:30:40');
INSERT INTO `lesson_presentation_slides` (`id`, `lesson_presentation_id`, `section`, `slide_type`, `slide_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(16, 3, 'learn', 'text', '{\"text\": \"<br>The graph below shows a proportional relationship between x and y.\\n<br>What is the constant of proportionality,&nbsp;<span class=\\\"katex\\\"><span class=\\\"katex-mathml\\\"><math xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\\\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\\\"true\\\" scriptlevel=\\\"0\\\"><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\\\"application/x-tex\\\">\\\\dfrac{y}{x}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\\\"katex-html\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><span class=\\\"base\\\"><span class=\\\"strut\\\" style=\\\"height:1.7936em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\\\"></span><span class=\\\"mord\\\"><span class=\\\"mopen nulldelimiter\\\"></span><span class=\\\"mfrac\\\"><span class=\\\"vlist-t vlist-t2\\\"><span class=\\\"vlist-r\\\"><span class=\\\"vlist\\\" style=\\\"height:1.1076em;\\\"><span style=\\\"top:-2.314em;\\\"><span class=\\\"pstrut\\\" style=\\\"height:3em;\\\"></span><span class=\\\"mord\\\"><span class=\\\"mord mathnormal\\\">x</span></span></span><span style=\\\"top:-3.23em;\\\"><span class=\\\"pstrut\\\" style=\\\"height:3em;\\\"></span><span class=\\\"frac-line\\\" style=\\\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\\\"></span></span><span style=\\\"top:-3.677em;\\\"><span class=\\\"pstrut\\\" style=\\\"height:3em;\\\"></span><span class=\\\"mord\\\"><span class=\\\"mord mathnormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-right:0.03588em;\\\">y</span></span></span></span><span class=\\\"vlist-s\\\">​ ?&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span class=\\\"vlist-r\\\"><span class=\\\"vlist\\\" style=\\\"height:0.686em;\\\"><br><img src=\\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" style=\\\"display: inline;\\\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>\"}', '2025-11-27 03:30:40', '2025-11-27 03:30:40'),
(17, 3, 'learn', 'text', '[]', '2025-11-27 03:30:40', '2025-11-27 03:30:40');
INSERT INTO `lesson_presentation_slides` (`id`, `lesson_presentation_id`, `section`, `slide_type`, `slide_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(18, 3, 'learn', 'text', '{\"text\": \"<h3><br></h3><div><img src=\\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></div>\\n<br><b>The graph shows the total cost for different weights of silver.</b>\\n<br><b>Fill in each blank. Use the graph to help you.\\n</b><br>1. When the weight is 0 pounds, the total cost is $______.  \\n<br>2. The graph passes through the point (______, ______). This is the origin.  \\n<br>3. The graph passes through the point (1, ______).  \\n<br>4. The constant of proportionality is ______ dollars per pound.  \\n<br>   (Hint: cost for 1 pound = ______ ÷ 1)  \\n<br>5. The point (2, 34) means 2 pounds cost $______.  \\n<br>   Price per pound = 34 ÷ ______ = $______.  \\n<br>6. The point (4, 68) means 4 pounds cost $______.  \\n<br>   Price per pound = 68 ÷ ______ = $______.  \\n<br>7. Because the graph is a _________________ that passes through _____________ and the ratio is always _________________,  \\n<br>   the relationship between weight and cost is __________________.  \\n<br>8. Write the equation that matches the graph (C = cost, w = weight in pounds):  \\n<br>   C = ______ × w  \\n<br>9. If someone buys 5 pounds of silver, the total cost will be $______.  \\n<br>   (Show work: ______ × 5 = ______)  \\n<br>10. If someone has $85, the maximum whole pounds of silver they can buy is ______ pounds.  \\n<br>    (Because ______ × ______ = 85)\\n<br>\\n<br><b>ANSWER KEY</b>  \\n<br><div><li>When the weight is 0 pounds, the total cost is $<strong>0</strong>.</li>\\n<li>The graph passes through the point (<strong>0</strong>, <strong>0</strong>). This is the origin.</li>\\n<li>The graph passes through the point (1, <strong>17</strong>).</li>\\n<li>The constant of proportionality is <strong>17</strong> dollars per pound.\\n(Hint: cost for 1 pound = <strong>17</strong> ÷ 1)</li>\\n<li>The point (2, 34) means 2 pounds cost $<strong>34</strong>.\\nPrice per pound = 34 ÷ <strong>2</strong> = $<strong>17</strong>.</li>\\n<li>The point (4, 68) means 4 pounds cost $<strong>68</strong>.\\nPrice per pound = 68 ÷ <strong>4</strong> = $<strong>17</strong>.</li>\\n<li>Because the graph is a <strong>straight line</strong> that passes through <strong>(0,0)</strong> and the ratio is always <strong>the same</strong>,\\nthe relationship between weight and cost is <strong>proportional</strong>.</li>\\n<li>Write the equation that matches the graph (C = cost, w = weight in pounds):\\nC = <strong>17</strong> × w</li>\\n<li>If someone buys 5 pounds of silver, the total cost will be $<strong>85</strong>.\\n(Show work: <strong>17</strong> × 5 = <strong>85</strong>)</li>\\n<li>If someone has $85, the maximum whole pounds of silver they can buy is <strong>5</strong> pounds.\\n(Because <strong>17</strong> × <strong>5</strong> = 85)</li></div>\"}', '2025-11-27 03:30:41', '2025-11-27 03:30:41'),
(19, 3, 'learn', 'text', '{\"text\": \"<h3>5 Multiple-Choice Questions from the Silver Cost Graph (Problem 8)</h3>\\n<br>\\n<br><b>Name: __________________________</b>\\n<br>\\n<br><b>Circle the correct answer.</b>\\n<br>\\n<br>1. According to the silver cost graph, what is the total cost for 0 pounds of silver?  \\n<br>   A) $17  \\n<br>   B) $34  \\n<br>   C) $0  \\n<br>   D) $68  \\n<br>   → <b>C</b>\\n<br>\\n<br>2. What is the constant of proportionality (price per pound) shown on the silver graph?  \\n<br>   A) $34  \\n<br>   B) $68  \\n<br>   C) $4  \\n<br>   D) $17  \\n<br>   → <b>D</b>\\n<br>\\n<br>3. The point (4, 68) on the silver graph means:  \\n<br>   A) 4 pounds cost $68  \\n<br>   B) $4 buys 68 pounds  \\n<br>   C) 68 pounds cost $4  \\n<br>   D) The price is $4 per pound  \\n<br>   → <b>A</b>\\n<br>\\n<br>4. Which statement is TRUE about the silver cost graph?  \\n<br>   A) The point (2, 34) means the price is $2 per pound  \\n<br>   B) The point (1, 17) shows the constant of proportionality  \\n<br>   C) The point (4, 68) means $4 buys 68 pounds  \\n<br>   D) The graph does NOT pass through (0, 0)  \\n<br>   → <b>B</b>\\n<br>\\n<br>5. How much would 6 pounds of silver cost according to this graph?  \\n<br>   A) $102  \\n<br>   B) $68  \\n<br>   C) $85  \\n<br>   D) $136  \\n<br>   → <b>A</b> (because 17 × 6 = 102)\\n<br>\\n<br><b>ANSWER KEY</b>  \\n<br>1. C 2. D 3. A 4. B 5. A\"}', '2025-11-27 03:30:41', '2025-11-27 03:30:41'),
(20, 4, 'learn', 'text', '[]', '2025-11-27 03:50:18', '2025-11-27 03:50:18');
INSERT INTO `lesson_presentation_slides` (`id`, `lesson_presentation_id`, `section`, `slide_type`, `slide_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(21, 5, 'learn', 'text', '{\"text\": \"<div style=\\\"align-self: center; display: flex; -webkit-box-flex: 1; flex: 1 1 0%; -webkit-box-orient: vertical; -webkit-box-direction: normal; flex-direction: column; max-inline-size: 100%; -webkit-box-pack: center; justify-content: center; padding-block-end: 1rem; color: rgb(48, 48, 48); font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;, &quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;; font-size: medium;\\\" class=\\\"chat-panel-empty-state ng-star-inserted\\\"><span style=\\\"block-size: 3rem; font-size: 3rem; inline-size: 3rem; cursor: pointer;\\\" class=\\\"xap-emoji-picker-trigger notebook-icon notebook-icon-editable ng-star-inserted\\\"><span style=\\\"padding: 0.3rem; background: none 0% 0% / auto repeat scroll padding-box border-box rgb(242, 242, 242); border-radius: 1rem;\\\" class=\\\"emoji-editable\\\">📈</span><div class=\\\"xap-emoji-keyboard\\\"></div></span><h1 style=\\\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-weight: 400; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 2rem; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;; letter-spacing: normal; margin-block: 0.75rem; color: rgb(37, 37, 38);\\\" class=\\\"notebook-title ng-star-inserted\\\">Ratios, Proportions, and Percent Applications</h1><span style=\\\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.25rem; font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, &quot;Google Sans&quot;, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.096px; display: inline-block; margin-block-end: 0.75rem;\\\" class=\\\"notebook-subtitle mat-body-small ng-star-inserted\\\">1 source</span><span style=\\\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5rem; font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, &quot;Google Sans&quot;, sans-serif; display: inline-block; margin-block-end: 0.75rem; overflow: auto;\\\" class=\\\"notebook-summary mat-body-medium\\\"><div style=\\\"line-height: 1.5rem; max-inline-size: 45rem;\\\" class=\\\"summary-content ng-star-inserted\\\"><p style=\\\"margin-block: 0px 0.75em;\\\">This collection of instructional excerpts and answer keys outlines practice problems across two primary middle-school mathematics units:&nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-weight: 600;\\\">proportional reasoning</span>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-weight: 600;\\\">percentage applications</span>. The first set of exercises requires students to analyze data presented in&nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-weight: 600;\\\">graphs and tables</span>&nbsp;to definitively identify whether relationships are proportional, often focusing on calculating the&nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-weight: 600;\\\">constant of proportionality</span>&nbsp;in real-world scenarios. The subsequent units shift focus entirely to percents, covering fundamental skills such as determining the&nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-weight: 600;\\\">part, whole, or percent</span>&nbsp;within diverse problems concerning taxes, commissions, and discounts. Finally, the practice material concludes by instructing users on how to calculate&nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-weight: 600;\\\">percent increase, percent decrease, and percent error</span>&nbsp;based on changes between original and new quantities.</p></div></span><div style=\\\"-webkit-box-align: center; align-items: center; display: flex; margin-block-end: 2rem;\\\" class=\\\"chat-panel-empty-state-action-bar ng-star-inserted\\\"></div><div style=\\\"-webkit-box-align: start; align-items: flex-start; align-self: stretch; display: flex; -webkit-box-orient: horizontal; -webkit-box-direction: normal; flex-direction: row; gap: 8px; inline-size: 676.975px;\\\" class=\\\"chat-panel-start-note-buttons ng-star-inserted\\\"></div></div><div style=\\\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: 16px; font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, &quot;Google Sans&quot;, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.096px; color: rgb(145, 145, 145); margin-block: 1rem; text-align: center;\\\" class=\\\"date-separator ng-star-inserted\\\">Today • 8:15 AM</div><div style=\\\"min-block-size: calc(100% + 1rem); color: rgb(48, 48, 48); font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;, &quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;; font-size: medium;\\\" class=\\\"chat-message-pair ng-star-inserted\\\"><div style=\\\"padding-inline-start: 2rem; display: flex; -webkit-box-pack: end; justify-content: flex-end;\\\" class=\\\"from-user-container\\\"><div style=\\\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5rem; font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, &quot;Google Sans&quot;, sans-serif; overflow-y: auto; white-space-collapse: preserve; margin-bottom: 0px;\\\" class=\\\"message-text-content mat-body-medium\\\"><div class=\\\"ng-star-inserted\\\" aria-level=\\\"3\\\" role=\\\"heading\\\"><p style=\\\"margin-block: 0px;\\\">from the file questions ideas but number not more than 50 with no fractions and dicimals :Quiz – Total 20 marks</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>5 Multiple Choice questions (4 options each) → 1 mark each = 5 marks</li>\\n<li>10 Matching questions (match expression to answer) → 1 mark each = 10 marks</li>\\n<li>5 Problem-Solving / Word Problems → 1 mark each = 5 marks</li>\\n<li>Provide full answer key with short explanations at the end.   ready to print.every option in new line so it is clear for the students</li>\\n</ul></div></div></div><div style=\\\"padding-inline-end: 2rem; padding-block-end: 1rem; display: flex; -webkit-box-pack: start; justify-content: flex-start;\\\" class=\\\"to-user-container\\\"><div style=\\\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5rem; font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, &quot;Google Sans&quot;, sans-serif; overflow-y: auto; white-space-collapse: preserve; margin-bottom: 0px;\\\" class=\\\"message-text-content mat-body-medium\\\"><div class=\\\"ng-star-inserted\\\"><div style=\\\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: 1.5rem; margin-block-end: 0.75rem;\\\" data-start-index=\\\"0\\\" class=\\\"paragraph normal ng-star-inserted\\\"><span class=\\\"ng-star-inserted\\\" data-start-index=\\\"0\\\">This quiz has been created based on the source material covering proportional relationships and percentage calculations, structured according to your requested format and constraints.</span></div><div style=\\\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 16px; line-height: 2rem; margin-block-end: 0.75rem;\\\" data-start-index=\\\"183\\\" class=\\\"paragraph heading2 ng-star-inserted\\\"><span class=\\\"ng-star-inserted\\\" data-start-index=\\\"183\\\">Quiz – Total 20 marks</span></div><div style=\\\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: 1.5rem; margin-block-end: 0.75rem;\\\" data-start-index=\\\"204\\\" class=\\\"paragraph heading3 ng-star-inserted\\\"><span class=\\\"ng-star-inserted\\\" data-start-index=\\\"204\\\">Section 1: Multiple Choice Questions (5 questions </span><span class=\\\"ng-star-inserted\\\"><span class=\\\"katex\\\"><span aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\" class=\\\"katex-html\\\"><span class=\\\"base\\\"><span style=\\\"height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;\\\" class=\\\"strut\\\"></span><span class=\\\"mord\\\">×</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\\\"ng-star-inserted\\\" data-start-index=\\\"260\\\"> 1 mark = 5 marks)</span></div><div style=\\\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none;